#14300
The Great Tower of Xerxes - Level 3~
This area (14301-14436) forms the 3rd level of the Great Tower of Xerxes.

The connection points are as follows:

North of 14301 connected to 14218.
Up of 14427 connected to 14501.

Mob Chutes:

14436 is the Master Chute.
14428, 14429, 14432, 14433, 14434 and 14435 are the other chutes.

While the lower levels are unfriendly to pass through at times, this is the
first level that will prove a major obstacle to groups with ambitions of
reaching the highest parts of the tower. There are many, MANY aggresive
mobiles here, quite a few of them with special routines specifically
designed to disrupt standard(dull) group orgainisations and methods. No
character could survive here alone, groups of characters venturing here
should have members of at least 35th level, here, no one is safe from
attack. The area is structured such that groups will have to wander all over
it in order to pass on, 3 keys(in sequence) being required. The first is
carried by a unique individual who loads into a random room, some where in
the maze. Because of the enviroment, tracking here is impossible, so
simply finding the first key could be a major under taking...

This area was written by Vex.
~
143 72 0 0 0 0 255 0
S
#14301
A stone corridor~
You are in a corridor of featureless stone. The stone of the corridor is 
continuous, showing no cracks or seams. Torches set in regular intervals
along the wall are the only thing breaking the monotony. The corridor 
continues to the south, while to the north the corridor ends in a spiral
stairway.
~
143 8 0 0 0 0 255 0
D0
The top of a spiral stair case is visible to the north.
~
~
0 0 14218
D2
The stone corridor continues to the south.
~
~
