#14310
Entrance to Darkness~
This is the end of a corridor of featureless stone. To the north you see an 
ornate archway, but beyond the arch, your light does not penetrate. In fact
it just appears to a black void, absorbing all light. If you dare, you can
enter the darkness to the north, the corridor continues to the east. There is
a plaque of brass here, covered in verdigris.
~
143 8 0 0 0 0 255 0
D0
You see only darkness...
~
~
0 0 14430
D1
The stone corridor continues to the east.
~
~
0 0 14309
E
ornate archway~
To your horror, you realise the arch is formed in the likeness of a rotting
human face. The eyes of the thing appear to be looking right at you, and when
they blink you realise the thing is "alive". A long moaning cry issues from 
its decayed mouth, but if its trying to tell you anything, its intelligble.
You wonder how such an abomination could be worked into stone, the thing
appears mindless, but you can feel its anguish.
~
E
brass plaque~
Brushing away the green verdigris, you are able to make out these words:
"Trial by Darkness"
~
S
#14311
Darkness~
The darkness seems to absorb light almost completely, even the enchanted 
sources in your possession shed but a dim glow, barely sufficient to see by. 
Horrific moans and terrified screams suddenly cut off echo through the dark. 
The air is bone-numbingly cold, sapping your strength. You can feel a cold 
stone wall to the north and south.
~
