#14372
Disorientation in the Darkness~
A sudden queasy feeling in the pit of your stomach strikes as soon as you
enter the room, then you seem struck by buffeting winds, but they subside to
quickly to do more than ruffle your hair. You quickly realise that the way you
came in no longer exists. You barely detect a faint light from the north, and
this appears to be your only exit.
~
143 73 0 0 0 0 255 0
D0
Peering through the darkness, you think the area opens up to your north.
~
~
